{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"edgeColoring()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeColoring","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/EdgeColoring.swift#L479","fileName":"EdgeColoring.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE04edgeC0AD04EdgeC0VyxGyF"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeColoring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/EdgeColoring"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is simple: no self-loops, no parallel edges."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructive proof. Edges in position order, each coloured through a fan at its end with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex available. At least Δ colours"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete graphs, Petersen), but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ vertices, each found among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory. For a multigraph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"digraph.undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edgecoloring()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/edgeColoring()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V","text":"EdgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructive proof. Edges in position order, each coloured through a fan at its end with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex available. At least Δ colours"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete graphs, Petersen), but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ vertices, each found among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory. For a multigraph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"digraph.undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()","title":"edgeColoring()","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edgecoloring()","role":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","title":"ColoringModule","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Gr